From 7766fa1ebf5a167e0ef7763c8b2777077c3f3d15 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nick Hainke <vincent@systemli.org>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 20:42:42 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] service: add per-instance 'vrf' option

Add a 'vrf' instance attribute which binds all sockets of the service
to a Linux VRF device, using ujail's new -v option.

Since ujail does the binding, setting 'vrf' starts the instance through
ujail even without a 'jail' table. Running the service outside of the
VRF could expose it to, or let it talk to, the wrong network, so the
instance fails to start if ujail is missing or 'trace' is set, which
bypasses ujail.

The ujail arguments for options outside the jail table (env, seccomp,
capabilities, user, ...) used to be counted in instance_jail_parse(),
which only runs if there is a jail table. Count them separately for
every jailed instance, otherwise an instance jailed only because of
'vrf' would overflow the argv array allocated in instance_run().

ujail creates the VRF cgroup below the instance cgroup, which then
can't be removed anymore. Remove empty child cgroups before removing
the instance cgroup.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Nick Hainke <vincent@systemli.org>
---
